
[38;5;231m⏺[39m Now the task model itself. This is less a fork than a shopping list, but each field you add is also a thing that can
  [3mchange[0m — and therefore a notification someone might get. So this list is effectively the menu of notification
  triggers.

  Baseline I'm assuming regardless: a task has a [1mtitle[0m, a [1mstatus[0m (open/done, or a small set), and a [1mcreator[0m. Those are
  table stakes.

  Two of the options below are heavier than they look:

  - [1mAssignee[0m is the single most valuable relevance signal in the whole design. "Assigned to me" is the clearest possible
    answer to "do I care about this." I'd take it even if you took nothing else.
  - [1mComments[0m are a sub-entity, not a field — separate records, their own ordering, their own permissions. They're also,
    in every real task app, the [3mdominant[0m source of notification volume. Including them roughly doubles sub-project one;
    excluding them means notifications will mostly be about status flips, which is a quieter product.

  Due date and priority/labels are genuinely cheap — plain fields on the task, and each just adds one more "changed"
  event.

  Pick what the product actually needs, not what sounds complete.
